WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.180
You have worked with a lot of extraordinary men.

2
00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:07.000
I mean Moneypenny, Bond, hello.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.168
I know.
(audience clap)

4
00:00:09.168 --> 00:00:13.751
Moneypenny, how about those extraordinary men?

5
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.740
I've been very, very lucky actually.

6
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.500
I've kissed some amazing men.

7
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.660
I mean, it's brilliant.

8
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.160
Another perk of the job.

9
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.050
It's a real great perk, isn't it?

10
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.360
It really is.
I love it.

11
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.890
There are some men you're more excited

12
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:28.723
to kiss than others.

13
00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:29.820
I will admit that.

14
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.908
There are lots of men I was excited to kiss,

15
00:00:31.908 --> 00:00:33.120
I have to admit.

16
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.445
That's my point!

17
00:00:34.445 --> 00:00:35.630
I love it.

18
00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.975
I mean, Idris Elba, for instance, it was amazing.

19
00:00:37.975 --> 00:00:40.949
(audience clap)

20
00:00:40.949 --> 00:00:41.917
Drew, can I just say

21
00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:44.175
that you're just getting everything out of me.

22
00:00:44.175 --> 00:00:45.854
Yes, yes!

23
00:00:45.854 --> 00:00:47.740
This topic, I'm like, we just started,

24
00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:48.760
where are we gonna go?

25
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.330
Is it true that you actually did get

26
00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:51.290
in a little bit of trouble

27
00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.330
for rumoring Idris Elba

28
00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.100
as the next Bond?
Oh yes, I did.

29
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.760
Yeah, it's a really dangerous thing

30
00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.480
when you answer the question, who's gonna be the next Bond?

31
00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.260 line:15%
I thought I'll just offer up a name.

32
00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.550 line:15%
I was working with Idris at the time,

33
00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:04.920 line:15%
so I said, Idris Elba.

34
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:05.753 line:15%
And then the title was,

35
00:01:05.753 --> 00:01:08.730 line:15%
"Naomi says Idris Elba to be next Bond."

36
00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:12.780
That went everywhere.
Did the broccoli family say?

37
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.570
No, they knew that I'd fallen into the journalist traps.

38
00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.400
Perfect, okay.
Yeah, that was okay.

39
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.000
But then Idris held it against me

40
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:19.833
'cause he was like,

41
00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:22.047
"In every interview, I have to answer questions

42
00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:23.890
"about being the next Bond."

43
00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:26.180
Sometimes I like weird avant garde questions.

44
00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.230
Will you play my favorite game with me?

45
00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:29.063
Okay, let's do it.

46
00:01:29.063 --> 00:01:34.063
Okay, in honor of your alien run-ins on your new show,

47
00:01:34.337 --> 00:01:36.670
"The man who fell to Earth",

48
00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.509
we're gonna play "The final five".

49
00:01:38.509 --> 00:01:41.899
(audience clap)

50
00:01:41.899 --> 00:01:43.750
Number one, what travel destination

51
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.320
would you bring an alien to here on Earth?

52
00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.070
I would take them to Costa Rica

53
00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:49.900
because I'm obsessed with Costa Rica

54
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.510
so they'd have to see it with me.

55
00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:52.343
All right, number two,

56
00:01:52.343 --> 00:01:54.860
have you ever witnessed anything extra terrestrial?

57
00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:55.693
I have not.

58
00:01:55.693 --> 00:01:58.410
I have to tell you, my mom and my stepdad,

59
00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.970
they go out a lot of nights with their deck chairs

60
00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.800
and they go to these secret locations where they hear

61
00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.000
that aliens have appeared

62
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.660
and they wait all night for them to appear.

63
00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.730
Were they excited for this role for you

64
00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.950
if they kind of love the other world?

65
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:14.980
They haven't seen it yet,

66
00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.570
but they're super excited about it.

67
00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.200
Yeah, it's totally their kind of thing.

68
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.033
Okay, number three,

69
00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:21.980
what human trait would you teach to an alien?

70
00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:26.290
I think the most important human trait is forgiveness.

71
00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.431
Where can we go without forgiveness?

72
00:02:27.431 --> 00:02:30.098
(audience clap)

73
00:02:32.493 --> 00:02:35.930
Of self as well, other people and of self.

74
00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:39.070
Okay, what is the first food that you would introduce

75
00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:40.220
to an alien?

76
00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.910
A green smoothie 'cause it's very healthy

77
00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:45.560
and I want them to be healthy and last a long time.

78
00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.591
And last but not least, would you ever date an alien?

79
00:02:48.591 --> 00:02:52.470
Absolutely, yes, no hesitation there!

80
00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:57.517
Thank you Naomi Harris.

81
00:02:57.517 --> 00:02:59.514
"The man who fell to Earth"

82
00:02:59.514 --> 00:03:04.020
is available April 24th on Showtime

83
00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:07.440
and I will say it is a magnificent show.

84
00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.100
It is really extraordinary.

85
00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.510
I think it's gonna turn heads

86
00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:11.780
and you guys are incredible in it,

87
00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.754
and it is really well done.

88
00:03:13.754 --> 00:03:15.496
Thank you so much.
Thank you so much.

89
00:03:15.496 --> 00:03:18.079 line:15%
(upbeat music)

